## Resolution

Pinned the actual MIT-declared TinyStories-260K/custom tokenizer and unchanged primary C test reference with revisions, hashes and notices. Added a bounded data-only decoder/import package and explicit scalar f64 profile for GQA, stored RoPE, RMSNorm, residuals, gated SiLU FFNs and a correctly shared embedding/output head. Byte-BPE has independently checked UTF-8/whitespace/fallback semantics. Source-bound transactional cache steps, uncached prefixes, limits, corrupt files/packages, no-overwrite outputs and small-artifact replacement boundaries are tested without changing existing block/graph limits.

At `63bdc538`, **57 Rust tests**, both portable release rlibs, all prior regressions and import/check/probe CLI passed on the NRL branch. Three actual-weight prompts match vectorized PyTorch f64 logits and FFN traces; original C float32 is checked under its separate tolerance. Nine tokenizer/decoding goldens match the primary C algorithm, and the complete oracle regenerates byte-identically. The real model has 260032 distinct parameters plus 4096 stored positional values. [Dated dense baseline](../nrl/reports/decoder-baseline-2026-10-26.json), [raw log](../nrl/reports/decoder-check-2026-10-26.txt), [contract](../nrl/specs/decoder-v0.md), [saved probe](../nrl/reports/decoder-probes-2026-10-26/0.json).

T06 is complete for this declared small decoder profile. This is not Qwen/native/GPU support or held-out language/compression evidence. The user explicitly authorized continuing T07–T10 without waiting for landing. Calibration, resumable local training, general metrics/benchmarks, mixed plans/search and student-activation adaptation remain under 900 and are executed next.
